  "id": "COMPOUND:20099 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "The compound (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one is implicated in the interaction with VMRC-MELG through multiple pathways. It is a target of Diplotrin A and Basiliskamide B, both of which are involved in the regulation of VMRC-MELG. Additionally, the compound acts as a target of CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is also a target of Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate. These findings suggest that the compound may influence VMRC-MELG through a series of enzymatic interactions, potentially affecting cellular processes involving sialylation and redox regulation. The evidence is consistent with a role in metabolic pathways, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
